.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Using a 1D model with 100 linear line elements, various ways of computing a fluid-static pressure are exercised using the compressible CO2 as the non-linear reference fluid\&.

.PP
Vertical integration of fluid pressure to obtain the absolute pressure as a function of depth is tried in different ways, comparing the results with thos obtained by top down integration\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
\fBTest\fP uses the model 'Greenshank_prism_mini' mini for the 3D testing\&.
.RE
.PP
